## 8. Self-correction on the theorem, case (iv), before publication of the note.
A first draft said that at ranks 39 and 41 degenerate order-2 conditions need s = 0 on >= 2 or 3 dimensions
(probability <= 7^-3).  WRONG: the corank-1 case at 7 far vertices (probability ~1/6) gives a condition whenever the
complementary plane C is anisotropic (rule (iii) of the note; (C43) is its rank-43 case).  Checked with o2_corank.py
(seeds 11, 12, 13; rho = 2, 4, 6): with C anisotropic, v7(det) - (6 - rho) in {3, 5} only (16/16, 6/6, 26/26); with
C hyperbolic, even values occur (180 + 8 + 1 of 232; 194 + 18 of 255).  See corank_*.json.

